{"name":"King Nacho","hex":"#ffb800","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"king","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male monarch; a man who heads a monarchy; in an absolute monarchy, the supreme ruler of his nation.","The monarch with the most power and authority in a monarchy, regardless of sex."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crown king, to make (a person) king.","To rule over as king."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king"},{"term":"nacho","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A single tortilla chip from a dish of nachos."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nacho"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nacho (footballer, born 1990)","blocks":[{"text":"José Ignacio Fernández Iglesias, known as Nacho Fernández or simply Nacho, is a Spanish professional footballer who plays as a defender for Saudi Pro League club Al-Qadsiah. Mainly a centre-back, he has also played at right-back and left-back on occasion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Nacho_Fern%C3%A1ndez_-_Ofrenda_de_la_Liga_y_la_Champions-56-L.Mill%C3%A1n_%2852109788795%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Nacho_Fern%C3%A1ndez_-_Ofrenda_de_la_Liga_y_la_Champions-56-L.Mill%C3%A1n_%2852109788795%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nacho_(footballer%2C_born_1990)","wikidata":"Q503137"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th